From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 21:10:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/panel: Add the Minimal Z10 e-paper display driver

Add a driver for the Minimal Phone MP01's e-paper display: a Pango
PGC4KL CPLD that takes 800x600 DSI video and updates the panel wherever
the frames change. The driver registers the DSI device on the host found
through the graph, runs the vendor's timing and power sequence, and
exposes the CPLD's two controls.

The vendor driver for this CPLD reprograms its flash from an embedded
bitstream at probe whenever the firmware is older than it expects, and
on a sysfs write. This driver reaches the CPLD only through a regmap
whose access tables cover the display registers 0x80-0x8f. Only the
waveform (0x8c, 0-3) and the clear command (0x8e = 0x05) are writable,
and the flash and configuration opcodes (0x10-0x71, 0xa1-0xa5, 0xff)
cannot be addressed at all. Reads use a separate write and read, as the
vendor's do, rather than a repeated start.

refresh_mode selects the waveform by behaviour: quality, clean, text or
fast. full_refresh runs the vendor's clear: clear, waveform 2, then the
selected waveform again 100 ms later. Both are interim sysfs until DRM
has a connector property for e-paper refresh.

The CPLD's power follows runtime PM. If the supplies are on at probe,
the bootloader is showing a picture, and the first prepare takes that
over without resetting the CPLD, as the vendor driver does. The panel
keeps its picture with the CPLD powered off.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
