diff --git a/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-panel-minimal-z10-eink b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-panel-minimal-z10-eink
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/Documentation/ABI/testing/sysfs-driver-panel-minimal-z10-eink
@@ -0,0 +1,28 @@
+What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/<bus>-<addr>/refresh_mode
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.0
+Contact:	Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
+Description:
+		(RW) The waveform the Minimal Z10 e-paper module drives
+		changes with. Reading lists the modes with the current one
+		in brackets; writing one of them selects it:
+
+		=======	=================================================
+		quality	full greyscale, slowest, least ghosting
+		clean	greyscale with less ghosting than quality;
+			switching to it flashes the panel twice
+		text	nearly two-level: crisp text, images lose greys
+		fast	fastest, most ghosting
+		=======	=================================================
+
+		The choice is kept while the display is off and applied
+		when it is next turned on.
+
+What:		/sys/bus/i2c/devices/<bus>-<addr>/full_refresh
+Date:		November 2026
+KernelVersion:	7.0
+Contact:	Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
+Description:
+		(WO) Writing 1 clears the panel with a full flashing refresh
+		that removes ghosting, then restores refresh_mode. Fails with
+		-EAGAIN while the display is off.
